    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'height' in a general, daily_life context typically refers to the vertical dimension of an object or person. While 'height' can sometimes mean 'altitude', '高度 (こうど)' specifically refers to 'altitude' or 'elevation' (e.g., of an airplane or mountain above sea level). This makes '高度' a narrower term than the general English 'height'. For a general learner, '高さ (たかさ)' is the more natural and common Japanese equivalent for the general concept of 'height' (of an object or building), and '身長 (しんちょう)' for a person's height.",
